{"kind":"report","text":"Decision on d072cb9b (planner, 2026-10-20): detached texts in offline replay.\n\n1. The archive stays free of texts. Export admission does not change (journal-path.ts:44 accepts no text). A text can be redacted later, and a Git archive cannot forget. So the archive holds no text bytes, and no caller supplies a text set. A clone stays self-contained.\n\n2. An omission record for each pass. For each detached text that an exported entry names, the pass records the text's digest, its UTF-8 byte count and the first exported entry that names it (scope and position). This is the existing omission inventory, with the byte count added. It holds no text bytes. A text that is already redacted at export has its tombstone in the journal, so it follows today's redacted path and has no omission row.\n\n3. Replay treats an omitted text as it treats a redacted one (verify.ts:25-28). It does not derive the text again. The report lists each omitted text under a new trust: \"each text that the archive omits: its digest, its byte count and the first entry that names it; nothing shows that the bytes were the text its digest names, or that they were within the bound of their field.\" Where a scope counts capacity, replay takes the byte count from the omission row as the text's known size, so the byte spans stay complete. Without that, they fall under incompleteBytes as today.\n\n4. Strict edges. A missing text that no omission row and no tombstone answers for still stops replay with incomplete, as today. An omission row that no exported entry names refuses the archive read. Where the journal itself records a text's size, the omission row must agree with it, or replay stops with mismatch.\n\n5. Privacy and budget. The archive adds only a digest, a byte count and a position for each text. Each costs a fixed amount of metadata in its pass, and a pass has at most as many rows as the texts its entries name.\n\n6. Witnesses on the test host. The four target replays reach consistent, and the report lists text 9e0a5a28 and any other omitted texts with their byte counts. Without its omission row, replay stops with incomplete at Directory 5. An extra omission row refuses the read. Each of these runs uses the native export path, not a mechanical copy.\n\n7. The /grow/ page and slice 9's text say that the archive holds no texts, and that offline replay takes the omitted texts on trust.\n\nNo deployment and no hosted read.","body":{"to":"builder"}}